wiretap-server (0.1.5) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * A batch the gateway refuses for its contents is kept in
    cache.dead-letter.db beside the disk cache, in the cache's own format,
    instead of being resent for ever and holding up everything behind it.
    Nothing is dropped: if that file cannot be written, the batch is cached
    and retried as before.
  * A batch sent in pieces that failed partway is no longer stored twice:
    only the pieces the gateway did not take are cached and resent.
  * An ACK for a batch other than the one sent is refused, and the batch is
    cached and retried.
  * A gateway whose database is not ready yet is logged as such (HELLO
    status 4), not as a bad database name.
  * A serial device's parity is read in any case ("Even" as well as "even").
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:53:24 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.4) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * CAN and serial lines are read through wiretap-lib-rs. An unplugged CAN
    adapter is read again when it returns, without a restart, and a loss is
    logged once rather than every second.
  * The serial line is now opened exclusively: while the server holds it,
    a second reader such as a debugging `cat` gets EBUSY. Stop the service
    before reading the line by hand.
  * A modbus-rtu device may name a catalogue of its vendor codes; see the
    shipped sungrow-rs485.catalog.toml. Optional; nothing changes without it.
  * Every frame the server has read before a stop is archived, and a
    stop no longer logs a spurious `queue FULL: size=0`.
  * A GVRET transmit declaring more than 8 bytes is refused, not cut to 8.
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:24:45 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.3) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * No change to the daemon. Republished alongside the gateway, which gains
    per-database events and schema v3, so the two halves stay on one version.
    A 0.1.2 daemon is served by a 0.1.3 gateway without complaint.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:13:12 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * A serial tap stamps each message when its last byte arrived, including
    the burst the framer releases once it has synced after an open; those
    used to share one timestamp. No configuration change; restart is all.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Fri, 12 Sep 2026 20:30:00 +0930

